cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use or adapt SFEXIS, credit Federico Vismarra, cite the preferred
  article below, and record the software commit used.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-13"
license: BSD-3-Clause
title: "SFEXIS: Strong Field Electron XUV Interaction Simulator"
authors:
  - family-names: Vismarra
    given-names: Federico
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2348-2749"
repository-code: "https://github.com/fedefirefox/SFEXIS"
url: "https://github.com/fedefirefox/SFEXIS"
abstract: >-
  MATLAB strong-field XUV/IR photoemission simulator retaining the original
  script workflow, full example scripts, and preserved original research sources.
  A separate AI companion provides a function-based version for automation.
  This bundle does not include the full ensemble averaging or retrieval
  implementation of the associated article.
  BSD-3-Clause covers the identified project-owned files; LICENSING.md records
  separately licensed helpers and unresolved bundled-material permissions.
keywords:
  - attosecond science
  - strong-field approximation
  - photoemission
  - attosecond streaking
  - MATLAB
  - XUV
  - RABBITT
  - photoelectron spectroscopy
  - scientific computing
